git-span placeholder. scripts/postinstall.js replaces this file
with the native binary for your platform. The name ends in .exe and the
first line intentionally has NO "#!" shebang so npm/yarn/pnpm cmd-shim
generates a direct-exec wrapper that runs on Windows; Unix ignores the
.exe suffix and execs by mode bit. This file is tracked NON-executable
(mode 644) on purpose: without a shebang, execvp()'s ENOEXEC fallback
would otherwise re-exec it via /bin/sh, which parses this very sentence
as a command line and recurses into itself indefinitely (a fork bomb —
see the git-span-fork-bomb incident report). Non-executable makes execvp
fail fast with EACCES instead. postinstall.js re-chmods to 0755 only
after replacing this text with the real binary. If you are seeing this
text, the postinstall step did not run.
